From 7e7342fd9b87efe9fcc17581fb26e38ddfde26b2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 17:09:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/10] .18 Reconciliation: required-vs-optional symbol
 handling for full coin universe

Same pattern as .13-.17, extended to this file's two-source (ledger +
observed-execution) verification: REQUIRED_SYMBOLS (BTC/ETH) remain the
only symbols whose structural invalidity, or evidence conflict, can block
or gate the whole reconciliation decision. Every other symbol either
source reports is reconciled independently.

Specific changes:
- New ledger_entry_reconciliation_errors_for_symbol() and
  observation_errors_for_symbol() helpers factor out the original
  per-symbol structural checks on each of the two upstream sources.
  verify_ledger() / verify_observed() now scope their per-symbol loop to
  REQUIRED_SYMBOLS only, as global gates.
- New reconcile_symbol() factors out the actual reconciliation decision
  logic (ledger-event x observed-status -> reconciliation_state) so it can
  be reused identically for required and optional symbols without
  duplicating the branching, returning both the decision dict and its
  state string for bucketing.
- build_reconciliation()'s main loop iterates every symbol either source
  reported (union with REQUIRED_SYMBOLS). Optional symbols get their own
  ledger/observation structural check first -- per this file's own
  fail-closed philosophy, a missing or invalid observation is never
  silently treated as reconciled, even for an optional symbol -- then the
  same reconcile_symbol() logic as required symbols.
- Deliberate aggregate design: reconciled_count/pending_count span the
  full symbol set (any symbol's clean reconciliation can make the overall
  RECONCILED, mirroring the any-symbol-can-signal pattern in .13-.17),
  but only REQUIRED_SYMBOLS conflicts gate overall_reconciliation to
  CONFLICT -- an optional symbol's own bad evidence blocks only that
  symbol (recorded in optional_symbols_blocked), never the whole cycle.
- main()'s missing-observation-file fallback path: its no_order_only
  check is now scoped to REQUIRED_SYMBOLS only (an optional symbol having
  an order intent must not affect it), and the resulting per-symbol
  UNVERIFIED decisions now also cover any optional symbols the ledger
  reported, each correctly reasoned (NO_OBSERVATION_SOURCE_FOR_NO_ORDER
  vs. NO_OBSERVATION_SOURCE_AVAILABLE) rather than silently dropped.
- print_report() iterates actual decisions instead of a fixed BTC/ETH
  tuple, labeling each symbol REQUIRED/OPTIONAL.

Adds 10 contract tests, including the required-conflict-gates-overall vs.
optional-conflict-does-not-gate distinction, and the missing-observation-
never-silently-reconciled behavior for an optional symbol. Full suite
(70 tests) green.

